  "rule": [
    "Label: post-freeze forward forecast v3; NOT part of the pre-registration (prereg-v2). Supersedes forecast v2 (tag forecast-v2) and v1 (tag forecast-v1), both kept unchanged, before any outcome was known.",
    "Snapshot: the Jodrell Bank glitch catalogue downloaded 2026-10-30 (MJD 61343); for each of the 21 included pulsars, its last catalogued glitch g. Pulsars whose g lacks dff > 0 or df1 > 0 are not forecastable.",
    "Forecast: ln T ~ Normal(mu, sigma), T = wait after g in days, from the frozen fits in results/primary.json: M2 mu = c_p + b ln R_g with R_g = (dff/1000)/df1; M0 (baseline) mu = c_p; each model's own sigma-hat. Median and central 50% (0.25-0.75) and 90% (0.05-0.95) windows of the conditional distribution.",
    "Scored set: a forecastable pulsar is scored only if (a) it is covered by the D4g Jodrell Bank rule; (b) it has no documented obs_end before MJD 61343 in data/meta/obs_end.csv (an obs_end equal to the last catalogued glitch epoch is the D4g placeholder, not a documented end of monitoring); and (c) 61343 - epoch(g) is no longer than its longest catalogued wait between consecutive glitches. Scored pulsars are conditioned on T > 61343 - epoch(g).",
    "Reported, not scored: every other forecastable pulsar, with the rules it fails and their numbers; conditioned on T > documented obs_end - epoch(g), or unconditioned if obs_end equals epoch(g).",
    "Scoring, on 2028-11-01 (MJD 62076): download the catalogue again. For each scored pulsar the outcome is the first glitch after g: the first catalogued glitch of that pulsar whose epoch exceeds g's epoch by more than g's catalogued epoch uncertainty (0 if none is given).",
    "Void: if that glitch's epoch is before MJD 61343, the pulsar is void and not scored.",
    "Score per scored pulsar: log predictive density of the observed wait (density of T in days) under the conditional forecast, or, if no glitch by MJD 62076, log of the conditional survival at the wait to that date; M2 minus M0. Total score = sum over scored pulsars; positive means M2 forecasts better.",
    "Coverage: for the 50% and 90% windows, the fraction of scored pulsars whose observed wait lies inside the window (ends included). A pulsar with no glitch by the scoring date counts as outside if the window ends before the scoring date, and as not determinable (excluded from that coverage) otherwise; the counts are reported.",
    "Functions: glitchlib.forecast (conditional_quantiles, log_predictive, coverage, outcome_for, forecast_window, scoring_eligibility)."
  ],
